# Offline and Sync

Purpose: client-side offline behavior per [`.cursor/api-contract.mdc`](../../.cursor/api-contract.mdc).

## Mandatory rules

- Connectivity is a hint, not proof of reachability.
- Queue offline drafts/pending writes in structured local storage when required.
- Sync operations idempotent where possible.
- Show sync states: pending, syncing, synced, failed, conflict.
- Do not silently discard offline changes.
- Conflict handling explicit; surface `409` with version metadata.
- Repositories expose consistent local + remote views.
- After HTTP writes succeed, expect matching domain events from the backend.
  Controllers reconcile through `WorkspaceSyncEngine`: apply safe typed deltas or
  perform the smallest HTTP refresh; widgets never consume raw websocket payloads.

## Online-only (never queue)

Auth/session changes, entitlement/break-glass approval, payments/refunds, mortuary release, final closeout — see `api-contract.mdc`.

## Sync queue fields

| Field | Purpose |
|---|---|
| local id | stable local reference |
| operation type | create, update, delete, upload |
| payload | serialized request |
| status | pending, syncing, failed, synced, conflict |
| retry count | retry policy |
| timestamps | ordering and diagnostics |

